.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-mash 1  "mash " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-mash \- The Snowball Showdown: pit two creatures against each other
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel mash\fR [\fB\-\-fast\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stage a three\-round showdown between two creatures. Each round tests strength, speed, cunning or dread, using each creature\*(Aqs stat card plus the roll of a die. Leave out one or both names for random contenders. Put a name of several words in quotes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fast\fR
Skip the dramatic pauses
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
Up to two creatures, e.g. krampus "yule cat"
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  terminal\-of\-tinsel mash
  terminal\-of\-tinsel mash krampus
  terminal\-of\-tinsel mash "yule cat" gryla \-\-fast
